comments.body:
@pdam-arista I reviewed this and the approach looks correct to me.

The skip is narrowly scoped to the passive-copper all-N/A case: it only triggers when there are no numeric CLI threshold rows, no numeric DOM threshold values, and every port with a DOM threshold row is identified as passive copper. That handles the false 0/0 threshold-match failure for passive DACs, while still failing for non-passive or unknown ports so optical threshold regressions are not hidden.

The mixed-platform behavior also looks intentional: if any port reports numeric thresholds, the test continues through the existing majority-match validation instead of taking the passive skip path. CI is green. No blockers from my side.
